{s:RC,k:'recap',term:'Recap',say:`Recap in three. Ripple walks the carry, two gate delays a bit; look-ahead builds every carry from g and p at once. Select, skip and save each cut the wait. And the numbers: sixty-four gate delays for thirty-two-bit ripple, fifteen units for skip.`,cues:{r1:'Ripple walks the',r2:'Select, skip and',r3:'And the numbers'},panels:[["Ripple and look-ahead","BLU",'vlRipple',['Ripple: carry-out at 2n gate delays.','Look-ahead: all cᵢ from g and p.'],'r1'],["Select, skip, save","ORG",'vlThree',['Select picks, skip jumps,','save postpones the carry.'],'r2'],["The key numbers","GRN",'vlNums',['32-bit ripple: 64 delays, 2.56 ns.','Skip with k = 4: 15 units, not 32.'],'r3']],live:[0,1,2]},
/* ---- exam practice ---- */
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"Why does a carry save adder not give a finished sum?",say:'Question one. Why does a carry save adder not give a finished sum?',cues:{k:'Question one',q:'Why does'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"Why does a carry save adder not give a finished sum?",say:`It never passes a carry across columns, so it leaves a sum vector and a carry vector. The value is S plus two C: a carry propagate adder must still add them.`,cues:{a1:'It never passes',a2:'The value is'},al:[["It gives a sum vector S and a carry vector C; no carry crosses columns.",'a1'],["The value is S + 2C, so a carry propagate adder must add S and the shifted C.",'a2']],vis:(c,u,b)=>`
${g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),VL_T(40,56,'from worked example 3',{fs:24,fw:700,fill:VL_GR})
 +VL_T(110,138,'S',{fs:28,fw:800,a:'end',fill:BLU})+VL_bits(130,100,['','1','0','0','0'],BLU,72)
 +VL_T(110,218,'C',{fs:28,fw:800,a:'end',fill:MAG})+VL_bits(130,180,['1','1','1','0',''],MAG,72)
 +VL_T(130,272,'two vectors, no sum yet',{fs:24,fw:700,fill:MAG}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),VL_arrow(310,290,310,330,INK,3)+VL_box(110,334,400,60,{st:GRN,sw:3,fill:'#E3FAF1'})+VL_T(310,372,'carry propagate adder',{fs:26,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:GRN})
 +VL_arrow(310,396,310,430,INK,3)+VL_T(310,470,'10110₂ = 22',{fs:30,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:GRN,mono:1}))}`},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"A column has g₀ = 0, p₀ = 1 and c₀ = 1. Find c₁.",say:`Question two. Given g zero is zero, p zero is one and c zero is one, find c one.`,cues:{k:'Question two',q:'Given g zero'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"A column has g₀ = 0, p₀ = 1 and c₀ = 1. Find c₁.",say:'Use the recurrence. c one is g zero plus p zero times c zero: zero plus one times one, which is one. The column passes the incoming carry on.',pause:.6,cues:{fk:'Use the recurrence',k1:'c one is',k1b:'zero plus one',k2:'The column passes'},calc:{f:['c₁ = g₀ + p₀c₀'],hint:'g₀ = 0, p₀ = 1, c₀ = 1',fk:'fk',steps:[["Substitute",["c₁ = 0 + 1·1","c₁ = 0 + 1·1 = 1"],["k1","k1b"]],["Meaning","c₁ = 1: the incoming carry propagates","k2"]],live:[0,1]}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"Why does a single-level look-ahead carry unit stop scaling beyond about 8 bits?",say:'Question three. Why does a single-level look-ahead carry unit stop scaling beyond about eight bits?',cues:{k:'Question three',q:'Why does'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"Why does a single-level look-ahead carry unit stop scaling beyond about 8 bits?",say:`The last carry holds a product of every p and c zero, so the widest gate needs n plus one inputs. In static ${P('CMOS')}, a wide AND means long series stacks: more delay, area and capacitance. Group generate and propagate keep every gate small, and the delay grows as a logarithmic tree.`,cues:{a1:'The last carry',a2:'In static',a3:'Group generate and'},al:[["cₙ holds pₙ₋₁pₙ₋₂…p₀c₀: the widest gate needs n + 1 inputs.",'a1'],["Static CMOS: a wide AND means long series stacks or gate chains, so more delay, area and capacitance.",'a2'],["Group generate and propagate keep gates small; the delay becomes a logarithmic tree.",'a3']],vis:(c,u,b)=>{
 const bar=(y,n,lab)=>VL_T(40,y+26,lab,{fs:22,fw:700,fill:VL_GR})+VL_box(140,y,n*10,36,{st:ORG,sw:2.5,fill:'#FFF1DF',r:6})+VL_T(n>20?150:150+n*10,y+27,n+' inputs',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:ORG});
 return `
${g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),VL_T(40,40,'widest AND in one look-ahead unit',{fs:24,fw:700,fill:INK})+bar(60,5,'4 bits')+bar(108,9,'8 bits')+bar(156,33,'32 bits'))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),VL_T(40,236,'33 inputs: a huge, slow gate',{fs:24,fw:800,fill:TRED}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a3'),VL_T(40,292,'instead: 4-bit blocks, a tree',{fs:24,fw:700,fill:GRN})
 +[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7].map(i=>VL_box(40+i*68,420,58,40,{st:GRN,sw:2,r:6})+VL_T(69+i*68,447,'4',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:GRN})).join('')
 +[0,1].map(i=>VL_box(110+i*272,350,140,36,{st:GRN,sw:2.5,fill:'#E3FAF1',r:6})+VL_T(180+i*272,375,'G, P',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:GRN})+[0,1,2,3].map(j=>VL_L(69+(i*4+j)*68,420,180+i*272,386,GRN,2)).join('')).join('')
 +VL_L(180,350,316,322,GRN,2)+VL_L(452,350,316,322,GRN,2)+`<circle cx="316" cy="318" r="9" fill="${GRN}"/>`)}`}},
{s:LS,k:'figs',term:'Your notes',title:'For your notes',say:`Your free notes are the PDF linked in the description. Redraw the look-ahead adder and the carry select figure from memory.`,cues:{t:'Your free notes',f:'Redraw the'},tags:[["Free notes for this lesson (PDF)", "link in the description"], ["In this lesson", "Adders: ripple carry and carry look-ahead; Carry select, carry save and carry skip adders"], ["Key terms and glossary", "at the end of the notes"]],figs:[["4-bit carry look-ahead adder", "a = 1011, b = 0110: each column forms g and p, the look-ahead unit makes c₁ to c₄ at once, and each sum is p ⊕ c. Result 10001₂ = 17."], ["Carry select on the same numbers", "The high block adds with carry-in 0 and 1 while the low block works; the real carry c₂ = 1 picks the carry-in-1 answer. Sum 17."]],note:"Sources your free notes draw on: Weste and Harris (CMOS VLSI Design); Rabaey, Chandrakasan and Nikolić (Digital Integrated Circuits); Kang and Leblebici (CMOS Digital Integrated Circuits); Parhami (Computer Arithmetic)"},
{s:OUT,k:'outro',term:'Outro',say:'So remember: ripple waits, look-ahead computes every carry at once, and select, skip and save each shorten the wait. Next time, array multipliers. See you there!',cues:{f:'So remember',w1:'ripple waits',w2:'look-ahead computes',w3:'and select, skip',n:'Next time',s:'See you there'},words:[['RIPPLE WAITS','BLU','w1'],['LOOK-AHEAD: ALL AT ONCE','ORG','w2'],['SELECT, SKIP, SAVE','GRN','w3']],next:["NEXT TIME", "Next lesson", "Array multipliers · Wallace tree and Booth multipliers", "book"],end:'See you there!'}
